{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788809558920484001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"fuchsia-wettish-leafbird","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"e411dec78080180854cb9719cdd827f2ef2330654665ce82fe9dc58b14821ffd","event_uuid":"793a6d51-a295-4a13-8d99-d491f3c584ce","position":{"commit_sha":"1a7c0fc71fe30e19dea8b272a28a7a85b80940d2","position":"1788805536816960159-793a6d51-a295-4a13-8d99-d491f3c584ce"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"1139f0f452e79f6ab7bbb2dfe9862d95daad9ad15e7ed1e1e40eb6cf1d372e56","event_uuid":"01a6d479-4e8b-4409-90f6-655d8045ec6a","position":{"commit_sha":"b8471f25c7c812f3f93b7dc7a0170a92ffb35f3f","position":"1788805580885763069-01a6d479-4e8b-4409-90f6-655d8045ec6a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e828ae34cb876d5fe0b278740120638e68611dc730e414b59f9463de019dc77f","event_uuid":"9ef0c3d4-d9b4-42d9-b1c4-1ac147ced98b","position":{"commit_sha":"473671db8fa97ec6819416ebd7b967cfaf62e58e","position":"1788805594372335577-9ef0c3d4-d9b4-42d9-b1c4-1ac147ced98b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"4d6938d6e802b4441d547b293d4e37ea3ed21ca77d14e3cd129bef2ce57ca83b","event_uuid":"0e173182-937a-4dea-947a-b97a3ce21265","position":{"commit_sha":"de66faaec28dd69d569e522261bcbe9fd85666ca","position":"1788805903056273174-0e173182-937a-4dea-947a-b97a3ce21265"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"9ee2e3550088f041abe333a4414606e9d78db51b27aa45b066d1e9bf6cf408da","event_uuid":"12bf9ac4-d6c6-4374-9fb6-e322fd099f5e","position":{"commit_sha":"ebca1e613da4b212d149bf84b1d0a60923198621","position":"1788807019587869566-12bf9ac4-d6c6-4374-9fb6-e322fd099f5e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation detail for this story (exact edit list; the description carries the decisions). Line numbers are on origin/main 2e81cb9767c1.\n\n4. `signature_findings` (`src/rebar/_engine_support/validate.py:70-142`): delete the `signing_key` try-block and `_NO_KEY` short-circuit (`:87-92`), drop `key=key` (`:124`); keep `mismatch -> major`, `foreign_key -> minor`; add `invalid` and `key_not_valid_at_era -> major`; `unsigned` and `certified` stay silent. Rewrite the docstring (`:71-81`).\n5. `_gen_local_files` (`src/rebar/_commands/init.py:480-495`): delete the `.signing-key` mint and the `import uuid` (`init.py:23`, sole use at `:491`); reword the comment to the `.closure-key` precedent (\"no longer minted; stays gitignored\"). Keep `.signing-key` in `src/rebar/_commands/_init_ensures.py:48` `_GITIGNORE` (existing stores carry the file; `.closure-key` at `:47` is the precedent).\n6. Keep `src/rebar/reducer/_present.py::_strip_hex` (`:56-70`): folded SNAPSHOTs still carry the hex and `rebar show` must strip it. Keep the nullable `signature`/`key_id` in `src/rebar/schemas/sign_result.schema.json:19-20` (read tolerance; reword \"RETIRED (story 8f1d)\" to \"RETIRED (2026-09): never emitted; pre-retirement records only\") and the `ticket_state.signature` mirror (operator ruling; `src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state.schema.json:164` prose \"the raw HMAC hex is stripped\" stays true).\n7. Docstring and prose sweep (no behaviour): `src/rebar/_signing_manifest.py:69-71`, `src/rebar/attest/__init__.py:7-12`, `src/rebar/attest/registry.py:22-24`, `src/rebar/attest/opcert.py:29-33,342`, `src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py:32`, `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py:567-571`, `src/rebar/_store/env_identity.py:14,188,276`, `src/rebar/_lib_identity.py:198`, `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py:186` (\"HMAC verify\" to \"op-cert verify\"), `src/rebar/reducer/llm_format.py:111`, `src/rebar/schemas/verify_signature_result.schema.json:5,20`.\n8. Docs: `docs/manifest-signing.md:56-60` becomes \"Legacy HMAC records (retired 2026-09)\": any `signature`-bearing record verifies `unsigned` with the retired reason; `docs/reuse-surface.md:144-155` delete \"Generic HMAC primitives\" and fix `:3,89,125,134`; `docs/attest-substrate.md:161-167`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md:593,1726`, `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md:154` (`unknown_scheme` to `unsigned`; keep the sentence containing \"HMAC-SHA256\" so `tests/unit/test_snapshot_docs.py:45-48` still passes), `docs/event-schema.md:51` (drop \"`verify_record` retains generic HMAC verification\"), `docs/exit-codes.md:202` (drop \"or, for a legacy HMAC record, a missing key\"), `docs/config.md:805` (drop `REBAR_SIGNING_KEY`), `docs/migrations/hmac-opcert-removal.md` (append \"## Retirement (2026-09)\" after `:85`; sections asserted by `tests/unit/test_hmac_opcert_removal_8f1d.py:179` stay), `docs/env-vars.md` regenerated with `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py` (the `REBAR_SIGNING_KEY` row at `:152` disappears).\n9. Baselines: `python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --update` (drops the entries at `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json:3632,3670,3713,3723,3755,3766,3782,3846,3989` plus `verify_record`); `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` passes (removed `env_var::REBAR_SIGNING_KEY` buckets as `stale`); `tests/golden/config_surface.json:17` `identity.signing_key` is the SSH authorship key and is untouched.\n10. ADR amendments. ADR 0044, append after the Context at `:10-13`: \"Amendment (2026-09): the symmetric HMAC model this ADR replaced is now fully retired: `src/rebar/_signing_hmac.py`, `REBAR_SIGNING_KEY` and `<tracker>/.signing-key` no longer exist; a non-envelope SIGNATURE record verifies `unsigned` with reason `legacy HMAC scheme retired (2026-09)`. The substrate below is the only signing path.\" ADR 0049, append to section 10 at `:176-182`: \"Contract completed (2026-09): the read-both window closed. `verify_attestation_record` dispatches envelope to the SSHSIG verifier and anything else to `signing.retired_scheme_verdict` (`unsigned`). No key custody remains for HMAC; a project holding a pre-2026-07-15 attestation on an open ticket re-runs the gate once (`rebar review-plan <id>`), the worst case being one re-review.\"\n\nTests to DELETE: `tests/unit/test_signing.py` HMAC functions (`:50-76`, `:91-160`, `:167-253`, `:257-311`; keep `:21-42`, `:84`, `:314`, `:331`; rewrite `:110-133` onto `retired_scheme_verdict`); `tests/unit/test_signing_module_split.py` (`:52-63` `MOVED_TO_HMAC`, `:74`, `:109-113` HMAC half, `:135-147`; drop `_signing_hmac.py` from the parametrize lists at `:150` and `:166`); `tests/unit/test_hmac_opcert_removal_8f1d.py::test_generic_hmac_utility_still_works_for_non_opcert` (`:99`); `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_signature.py::test_injected_env_key_round_trips` (`:146-153`) and `::test_readonly_verify_does_not_mint_key` (`:257-267`); `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_attested_signing.py::test_payload_version_unchanged` (`:57-58`); `tests/scripts/test_residual_drain_seam_clean_heldout.py::test_signing_key_env_injection_is_preserved` (`:187-193`); `tests/unit/test_canonical_consolidation.py` (`:43-49`, `:110-111`, `:136-146`); `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_signing_key_keeps_restrictive_mode` (`:202-205`); `tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py:311-314`.\n\nTests to REWRITE: `test_hmac_opcert_removal_8f1d.py`: `_write_legacy_hmac_opcert` (`:116`) builds the record as a literal; `:148` `unknown_scheme` becomes `unsigned` plus `\"retired\" in reason`; these survive as the new contract: `:52`, `:62`, `:75` (registry has no HMAC scheme), `:88` (sign_manifest emits no `signature`/`key_id`), `:154` (record byte-unchanged on disk), `:164` (re-running the gate certifies), `:179`, `:195`. `tests/unit/test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py:308-324` literalise plus `unsigned`; delete `:398-405`. `tests/unit/test_opcert_storage_heldout.py:98-118` literalise, `:148` becomes `unsigned`. `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_attestations_integration.py:166` assert `unsigned`. `test_signature.py:187-226` build the two racing events with `sign_manifest`. `test_attested_signing.py:86-96` compare two `sign_manifest` envelopes. `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py:188` drop `.signing-key`. `tests/_topology_template.py:20` and `tests/interfaces/_store_template.py:30` drop the `.signing-key` tuple. `tests/unit/store/test_stamped_lock.py:340` remove the `\"_signing_hmac.py\": 2` key.\n\nTests to TOUCH (delete one `monkeypatch.setenv(\"REBAR_SIGNING_KEY\", ...)` line each): the 34 files listed by `git grep -ln 'REBAR_SIGNING_KEY' -- tests` (for example `tests/unit/_audit_page_helpers.py:29`, `tests/unit/test_fixture_heal.py:53`, `tests/integration/reviewbot_convergence_support.py:64`).\n\nTests untouched: `test_mcp_auth_jwks.py` (JWT), `test_check_ssm_secret_state.py`, `test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py`, `test_identity_ts3_117b*.py` (`identity.signing_key` is the SSH authorship key; the enum at `:247-266` is unchanged), `test_attest_registry_heldout.py:79`, `test_opcert_cross_environment_c21f.py`, `test_attestations_reducer.py:23` and `test_legacy_signature_mirror_drop.py:25` (opaque legacy shapes; keep).\n\nNEW `tests/unit/test_hmac_retirement.py`: fixture reused from `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_attestations_integration.py:150-180` (`append_event(resolved, \"SNAPSHOT\", {\"compiled_state\": ..., \"source_event_uuids\": ..., \"compacted_at\": 1}, tracker)`), with `compiled_state[\"attestations\"][\"plan-review\"]` set to the exact live shape of `.tickets-tracker/003d-e6b0-9e58-4b52/1785993218769510001-a91e47c6-880d-42f5-b492-247181da8bf3-SNAPSHOT.json`: keys `algorithm: \"HMAC-SHA256\"`, `author`, `head_sha`, `key_id: \"412fa5372ad877e0\"`, `kind: \"plan-review\"`, `manifest: [\"plan-review: PASS\", \"ticket: <id>\", \"material: 5e6cba9142ddb7e2\", ..., \"verified-at-sha:2272d68c...\"]`, `signature: <64 hex>`, `signed_at: 1783806358702652000`. Tests: (a) `reduce_ticket` returns the map and `rebar.show_ticket` renders `attestations[\"plan-review\"]` without `signature`; (b) `rebar verify-signature <id> --kind plan-review --output json` exits 1 with `verdict == \"unsigned\"`, `reason` containing `\"legacy HMAC scheme retired\"`, `key_id == \"412fa5372ad877e0\"`, `step_count == len(manifest)`; (c) `plan_review_status(id)` returns `verdict == \"unsigned\"` and the reason text (via `attest_gate.py:136-147`); (d) `signature_findings(tracker)` returns `[]`; (e) `monkeypatch.setenv(\"REBAR_SIGNING_KEY\", \"x\")` changes nothing and `scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check` stays green; (f) `test_no_hmac_readers_remain`: `git grep -E 'signing_key\\(|REBAR_SIGNING_KEY|compute_signature|verify_record\\b' -- src` is empty.","timestamp":1788805580885763069},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Baseline maintenance step required in this change (verified on origin/main): `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py::test_the_committed_baseline_matches_the_live_tree` asserts `set(baseline) | admitted == live`, so removing `REBAR_SIGNING_KEY` leaves a stale `env_var` row that `scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` tolerates but the pytest does not. Run `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` after the removal and commit the resulting `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` (it refuses while `new>0`). Precedent: commit 81da792. This is the operator-sanctioned path for this epic.","timestamp":1788805903056273174},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Cross-epic ownership note (test-suite epic sainted-illjudged-fossa, story S1): that story DELETES `tests/unit/test_signing_module_split.py` and `tests/scripts/test_residual_drain_seam_clean_heldout.py` whole (they are one-time split guards). This story's file impact edits both (\"drop hmac seam\", \"drop env test\"). Landing rule: if the test-suite story has already landed, both files are gone and this story makes no edit to them (drop the two rows from the change); if this story lands first, apply its edits as planned and the test-suite story deletes whatever remains. Neither story waits on the other.","timestamp":1788807019587869566}],"created_at":1788805536816960159,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/_signing_hmac.py` (276 LOC) keeps key custody, payload canonicalisation, `compute_signature`, and `verify_record` alive so the dispatcher can still verify a symmetric scheme that mints nothing: the 3,883 live SIGNATURE events on this tracker are all Ed25519 op-certs, and `sign_manifest` (library; CLI `rebar sign` at `src/rebar/signing.py:353-391`; MCP `sign_manifest` at `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:501-514`) mints only through `mint_opcert_record` (`signing.py:218`). A record of an op-cert kind already reads NOT-certified (`_hmac_opcert_not_certified`, `_signing_hmac.py:259-276`), but `REBAR_SIGNING_KEY` and `<tracker>/.signing-key` are still read on every verify (`signing.py:157,268,278`), `rebar init` still writes a secret nobody uses (`src/rebar/_commands/init.py:488-495`), and the generic non-op-cert HMAC path (`signing.py:156-158`) is reachable by no producer. The 688 folded SNAPSHOTs carrying HMAC entries (1,124 entries on closed or deleted tickets, 1 on an open ticket) must keep reducing and rendering; they must simply verify as `unsigned`. The reducer folds `attestations[kind]` dicts verbatim (`src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py:556-559`) and never imports `_signing_hmac`. Three HMAC readers remain (`signing.py:151-158`, `signing.py:268,278`, `src/rebar/_engine_support/validate.py:88-91`); no doctor or fsck module reads the key file. `foreign_key` and `unknown_scheme` remain live op-cert and registry verdicts (`src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py:282,293,308`; `src/rebar/attest/registry.py:108`), so the `verify_signature_result.schema.json:17` enum and `types.py:361-371` Literal do not change. Operator decision (2026-09-06): retire fully. Cites are on origin/main 2e81cb9767c1.\n\n## Approach\n1. Replacement function in `src/rebar/signing.py`, replacing the import block at `signing.py:40-51`:\n```python\nLEGACY_HMAC_ALGORITHM = \"HMAC-SHA256\"   # recognised on read only; never minted\nHMAC_RETIRED_ON = \"2026-09\"\n\ndef retired_scheme_verdict(record: dict | None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Uniform NOT-certified verdict for any non-envelope SIGNATURE record. Same base keys\n    as the op-cert verdict (_opcert_verify.py:225-241) so compute_validity /\n    signature_findings / plan_review_status read it unchanged; never raises.\"\"\"\n    record = record if isinstance(record, dict) else {}\n    raw = record.get(\"manifest\")\n    manifest = raw if isinstance(raw, list) else []\n    key_id = record.get(\"key_id\")\n    legacy = bool(record.get(\"signature\")) or record.get(\"algorithm\") == LEGACY_HMAC_ALGORITHM\n    return {\n        \"manifest\": manifest, \"step_count\": len(manifest),\n        \"algorithm\": record.get(\"algorithm\"),\n        \"key_id\": key_id if isinstance(key_id, str) else None,\n        \"signed_at\": record.get(\"signed_at\"), \"head_sha\": record.get(\"head_sha\"),\n        \"verified_at_sha\": verified_at_sha_from_manifest(manifest) or record.get(\"verified_at_sha\"),\n        \"rebar_version\": rebar_version_from_manifest(manifest), \"trust_basis\": None,\n        \"verified\": False, \"verdict\": \"unsigned\",\n        \"reason\": (f\"legacy HMAC scheme retired ({HMAC_RETIRED_ON}); re-run the gate to mint an op-cert\"\n                   if legacy else \"ticket has no signature\"),\n    }\n```\n2. `verify_attestation_record(record, ticket_id, *, kind=None, repo_root=None)` (`signing.py:119-158`): drop the `key` kwarg and the `attestation_kind` import; body becomes envelope -> `verify_opcert_record(...)`, else `retired_scheme_verdict(record)`. `OPCERT_KINDS` (`signing.py:115`) stays (imported by `src/rebar/_commands/remote_cert.py:22`, `src/rebar/opcert_service/jobs.py:32`).\n3. `_resolve_and_reduce` (`signing.py:246-278`) returns `(resolved, state)`; `verify_signature` and `verify_attestations` (`signing.py:325-349`) stop passing `key=`. Delete the legacy render branch in `sign_cli` (`signing.py:384-390`, reads `record['key_id']`/`['signature']`, unreachable). Rewrite the module docstring (`signing.py:1-22`) and `__all__` (`signing.py:74-109`): remove `ALGORITHM`, `PAYLOAD_VERSION`, `_NO_KEY`, `_canonical_payload`, `_generate_key_file`, `_hmac_opcert_not_certified`, `compute_signature`, `key_fingerprint`, `signing_key`, `verify_record`; add `retired_scheme_verdict`, `LEGACY_HMAC_ALGORITHM`, `HMAC_RETIRED_ON`.\nSteps 4 to 10 (validate.py, init.py, kept read-compat, the prose sweep, docs, baselines, ADR amendments) and the exact test delete/rewrite/touch lists are in this ticket's first comment.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/_signing_hmac.py` (delete); `src/rebar/signing.py`; `src/rebar/_engine_support/validate.py`; `src/rebar/_commands/init.py`; the nine prose files in step 7; `src/rebar/schemas/sign_result.schema.json`; `src/rebar/schemas/verify_signature_result.schema.json`; the ten docs in step 8; `docs/adr/0044-asymmetric-attestation-substrate.md`; `docs/adr/0049-opcert-asymmetric.md`; `docs/release-notes.md`; `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json` (regenerated); tests below. Out of scope: `.gitignore` (only `infra/compose/*signing-key` lines, unrelated), `infra/**` (`MCP_HMAC_SIGNING_KEY` and the SSO cookie HMAC are different secrets), `docs/security.md` (no mention), `_present.py`, the `ticket_state.signature` mirror.\n\n## Testing\nHappy: `pytest tests/unit/test_hmac_retirement.py tests/unit/test_signing.py tests/unit/test_signing_module_split.py tests/unit/test_hmac_opcert_removal_8f1d.py tests/unit/test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py tests/interfaces/lifecycle -q`; `python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --check`; `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check`; `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check`; `rebar init` in a temp repo followed by `test -e .tickets-tracker/.signing-key` fails. Edge: non-list `manifest` gives `step_count 0` and `unsigned`; a `signature`-bearing record whose `manifest[0]` is `custom: x` gives `unsigned` (no generic path); a map with HMAC `plan-review` plus a fresh op-cert `completion-verifier` gives `unsigned` and `certified` respectively; `verify_attestation_record(None, id)` gives `reason == \"ticket has no signature\"`. `make verify` before push.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_signing_hmac.py` is absent and `git grep -E 'signing_key\\(|REBAR_SIGNING_KEY|compute_signature|verify_record\\b' -- src` prints nothing (asserted by `test_hmac_retirement.py::test_no_hmac_readers_remain`).\n- [ ] `verify_attestation_record` has no `key` parameter and `retired_scheme_verdict` is exported; `python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] The 003d-shaped SNAPSHOT fixture reduces, renders, and verifies `unsigned` with the retired reason on the CLI, on MCP `verify_signature`, and on `plan_review_status` (tests a to c pass).\n- [ ] `rebar init` no longer writes `.signing-key` and `.signing-key` remains in the tracker `.gitignore` (test in `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py`).\n- [ ] `signature_findings` emits nothing for a store of HMAC-only records (test d).\n- [ ] `docs/env-vars.md` has no `REBAR_SIGNING_KEY` row; ADR 0044 and 0049 carry the amendment paragraphs; the release note is present and `tests/unit/test_hmac_opcert_removal_8f1d.py::test_migration_doc_present_and_documented` asserts the \"Retirement (2026-09)\" heading.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.\n\nRelease note (BREAKING, pre-1.0): the legacy HMAC-SHA256 signing scheme is retired. `REBAR_SIGNING_KEY` and `<tracker>/.signing-key` are no longer read (`rebar init` stops creating the file; delete yours); every SIGNATURE record without a DSSE `envelope` (all attestations minted before 2026-07-15) now verifies `unsigned` with reason `legacy HMAC scheme retired (2026-09); re-run the gate to mint an op-cert`, no longer `unknown_scheme` or `foreign_key`; closed tickets are unaffected; an open ticket holding one needs one `rebar review-plan`; `rebar.signing.{signing_key, key_fingerprint, compute_signature, verify_record, ALGORITHM, PAYLOAD_VERSION}` are removed from the library surface and `verify_attestation_record` loses its `key` parameter.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_signing_hmac.py","reason":"delete"},{"path":"src/rebar/signing.py","reason":"retired_scheme_verdict; drop HMAC imports/key kwarg"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/validate.py","reason":"signature_findings without a key"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/init.py","reason":"stop minting .signing-key"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/sign_result.schema.json","reason":"prose"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/verify_signature_result.schema.json","reason":"prose"},{"path":"src/rebar/_signing_manifest.py","reason":"comment"},{"path":"src/rebar/attest/__init__.py","reason":"docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/attest/registry.py","reason":"docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/attest/opcert.py","reason":"docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py","reason":"docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py","reason":"tool docstring :567-571"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/env_identity.py","reason":"docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_identity.py","reason":"docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py","reason":"docstring :186"},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/llm_format.py","reason":"docstring"},{"path":"docs/manifest-signing.md","reason":"rewrite legacy section"},{"path":"docs/reuse-surface.md","reason":"delete HMAC primitives"},{"path":"docs/attest-substrate.md","reason":"scope note"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"verdict wording"},{"path":"docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md","reason":"verdict wording"},{"path":"docs/event-schema.md","reason":"SIGNATURE row"},{"path":"docs/exit-codes.md","reason":"verify-signature row"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"secrets list"},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"regenerated"},{"path":"docs/migrations/hmac-opcert-removal.md","reason":"retirement section"},{"path":"docs/adr/0044-asymmetric-attestation-substrate.md","reason":"amendment"},{"path":"docs/adr/0049-opcert-asymmetric.md","reason":"amendment"},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"BREAKING entry"},{"path":"tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json","reason":"regenerated"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_hmac_retirement.py","reason":"new"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_signing.py","reason":"delete HMAC tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_signing_module_split.py","reason":"drop hmac seam"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_hmac_opcert_removal_8f1d.py","reason":"unsigned contract"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py","reason":"literal records"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_storage_heldout.py","reason":"literal records"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_signature.py","reason":"op-cert events"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_attested_signing.py","reason":"envelope compare"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_attestations_integration.py","reason":"unsigned"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py","reason":"no key file"},{"path":"tests/_topology_template.py","reason":"identity files"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/_store_template.py","reason":"identity files"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_canonical_consolidation.py","reason":"drop sign goldens"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py","reason":"drop param pins"},{"path":"tests/unit/store/test_stamped_lock.py","reason":"survivor map"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_residual_drain_seam_clean_heldout.py","reason":"drop env test"},{"path":"tests/","reason":"34 files: delete one setenv(REBAR_SIGNING_KEY) line each (git grep -ln REBAR_SIGNING_KEY -- tests)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","d6e8-0730-22df-45a8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"d6e8-0730-22df-45a8","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_id":"3662-1631-4300-4390","ticket_type":"story","title":"Delete _signing_hmac.py; every non-envelope SIGNATURE record reads unsigned with the retired-scheme reason","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["793a6d51-a295-4a13-8d99-d491f3c584ce","01a6d479-4e8b-4409-90f6-655d8045ec6a","9ef0c3d4-d9b4-42d9-b1c4-1ac147ced98b","0e173182-937a-4dea-947a-b97a3ce21265","12bf9ac4-d6c6-4374-9fb6-e322fd099f5e"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788809558920484001,"uuid":"db502543-3f08-4fe7-b213-e285f7b461a1"}